ctor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|3|=3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281403 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b77f94-9b2e-5986-9a43-c22541a1c39b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278743} {:answer/id #uuid "7a11c398-9165-5c5e-b795-7af0e1679f50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279680} {:answer/id #uuid "94ee1b63-9a47-5ca7-aacf-a87f30e1d00e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279915} {:answer/id #uuid "95d85816-8b14-528a-a28e-a8e5a48909b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279922} {:answer/id #uuid "fffb02da-41f7-5223-94e2-b3b8c0b034e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279915} :answer-field/id #uuid "523714f3-7d37-5296-ad4e-2a05740f19bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280967}] :question/id #uuid "faa815d3-1a15-5270-95c0-06e76987590b" :question/math-academy-id "q-162193" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+5v+2,\\,y=1-u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+5v+2 \\\\ 1-u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+5v \\\\ -u\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 5=5.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|5|=5.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1283e1d9-5638-5cf5-8afe-fccb48c4513e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278761} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e99c71-ce7b-5a57-8b35-eff03f28886a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280088} {:answer/id #uuid "bee5e71a-fc3b-5642-9353-bcf840af6970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280271} {:answer/id #uuid "d650e02b-bf8f-5b88-a546-cd6aa55f62f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280483} {:answer/id #uuid "e733f81f-7e5b-56da-a2cd-22f5cd7afff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280483} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f5d13f4-2cb9-5ffa-b608-20e5bb1d0372" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280960}] :question/id #uuid "79b6b1e2-201b-5b88-aae8-abebb7edf5f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-162195" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-2v-3,\\,y=u-v+2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2u-2v-3 \\\\ u-v+2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2u-2v \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}=2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|0|=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c17750-e31e-532b-ae8d-7979de4d8d78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372002} {:answer/id #uuid "ad0c1dd5-b9ea-567c-a97b-f4096b3e1a5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372003} {:answer/id #uuid "5e0e426b-b2e9-58a1-91ce-578d1bd6cc16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372004} {:answer/id #uuid "1a41d7c7-bfb3-558c-bcd5-8d233c807fdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372005} {:answer/id #uuid "681b6932-d634-563f-b59e-a68a14cc53c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372006} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2e7db5e-75b3-5228-9ad8-cef0891cba6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372001}] :question/id #uuid "d122e060-ffdf-5149-8bb7-a8a052fb44e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162172" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}=2\\cdot (-1)-3\\cdot 1=-5.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-5|=5.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dd51353-621e-56ae-bd7e-c1dcf4750e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372009} {:answer/id #uuid "4692f893-08bf-51dc-8c1d-be1f128421c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372010} {:answer/id #uuid "dc922160-ef0e-51c1-bb3d-1ca4475e6dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372011} {:answer/id #uuid "b3632d7d-0532-52f8-932d-ff5cdd002973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372012} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9caf61-79c1-50ad-a6f3-d6e5f8d0d815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372009} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab22a8ca-8854-500e-8a30-6e7d2bafc9e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372008}] :question/id #uuid "7d4e1db4-c725-5d09-875d-b4ebdbd932b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-162175" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|3|=3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bc4fab2-f286-5943-a45f-a20492b01ffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417824} {:answer/id #uuid "76b47f26-b551-5ab2-a16b-a5772ef735ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417827} {:answer/id #uuid "ca24dbee-3bf2-5067-b768-9753b1ef80ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417831} {:answer/id #uuid "d2847d2c-57b6-59e8-b9ce-cd6f7d5c8fab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417832} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b0cc75-4660-5f89-b375-205d3cc92d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417827} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc6bf158-bc5a-5b83-aecb-e172b7a9b66e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417835}] :question/id #uuid "914af94d-7042-54e6-acb1-fed694c9a4de" :question/math-academy-id "q-162181" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-2|=2.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area Scale Factor of an Affine Transformation"}] :topic/math-academy-id 3706 :topic/title "The Image of an Affine Transformation"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060657} :activity/id #uuid "d6d1f64b-2ca1-5bc1-b04e-f255dfa6a0e3" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060657 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060933 :tutorial/content "We can calculate the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ using the following five-step algorithm.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant $\\det(A)$ of the matrix.\n\n**Step 2:** Form the **matrix $M$ of the minors** of $A,$ where each entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ is replaced by its minor $M_{ij}\\mathbin{:}$\n   ![](images/14/14905267240a1e8eb7f54ae47b813c24aa5eb26415c419bbd0ec53425693309b.svg)\n\n**Step 3:** Create the **matrix $C$ of cofactors** by changing the sign of some entries of the matrix of the minors according to the **rule of alternating signs**:\n   \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}+ & - & + \\\\ - & + & - \\\\ + & - & +\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFor each entry of $M$, we change the sign if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$-$\". Otherwise, if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$+$\", then we don't change the entry.\n\nSo, the matrix of cofactors is given by\n\n![](images/a5/a57831b81711ce44dc46c2a3a91b18d8dbfe4078697805369097421351294d2e.svg)\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors, $C^T.$\n\n![](images/e9/e93df3291f387eaac0f6992b38e005f72b08b71b99c7cef8fe6a3b8f42662ebc.svg)\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix:\n   \n\n$$\nA^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{\\det ( A)}C^{T}\n$$\n\nIn other words, we divide each entry of the transpose of the matrix of cofactors by the determinant of the original matrix (which we computed in step 1).\n\nLet's see this in practice, in the next example." :tutorial/id #uuid "9c7ba5cd-b4b2-595b-bbad-dfbdac248280" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3051 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "40317ef1-e2cc-5e12-bdbe-2a42b66c8d16" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060658}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060658 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330"} :step/id #uuid "fc1a94a9-263e-5e41-a86c-15959c3a9e6e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060660}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060659 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172"} :step/id #uuid "902e05e9-d18d-5cea-b49d-e1ac3fd78059"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060660 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060934 :tutorial/content "We make the matrix $C$ of cofactors by changing the sign of alternate entries of the matrix $M$ of the minors. So, each entry $c_{ij}$ of $C$ equals\n\n$$\nc_{ij} = (-1)^{i+j} M_{ij},\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the minor of the entry $a_{ij}$ in the matrix $A.$\n\nWith this and the formula for the inverse, we can write the formula for each entry $a'_{ij}$ of the inverse matrix $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n$$\na'_{ij} = \\dfrac{1}{\\det(A)}c^t_{ij}\n        = \\dfrac{1}{\\det(A)} c_{ji}\n$$\n\nHere, we used the fact that the entry $c^t_{ij}$ of $C^T$ is equal to the entry $c_{ji}$ of $C$ by the definition of the transpose." :tutorial/id #uuid "835c9ab0-dbce-5297-9a57-3978df178fa3" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3052 :tutorial/title "Calculating Individual Entries of the Matrix of Cofactors"} :step/id #uuid "b8784f82-7077-5c6e-b26b-f9e36420e73c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060661}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060661 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7"} :step/id #uuid "cb81629b-755e-56a7-88e6-963569b9be54" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060659}}] :activity/title "Calculating the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Using the Cofactor Method" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059887}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186049043 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059754 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059563 :question/id #uuid "8cd94856-fbe5-53a4-b7f2-f5b29b7aa927" :question/math-academy-id "e-4514" :question/problem "Find the inverse of ![](images/89/8967a472cff03599b1c2c94704fc9dc7272dc2a344d1876309dce1010a7ecc1f.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-(8-12)+2(-3-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 14 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n![](images/51/51ba8948d60b649bea88218e86b2ea39cbecfe8014367a3def09d2aeb7667460.svg)\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/b6/b6339df9152864283a9ed0b938c2183da94121edec8d5b434566b2953e5bd0b0.svg)\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{9}{2} & 7 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & -2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98a8da6d-1175-5690-993a-43baccf86886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & -7 \\\\ 9 & 34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059311} {:answer/id #uuid "f014818e-2156-5a3a-87fa-7de07564038f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -17 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059312} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb55f38-7b19-5ec2-a20e-0619df019195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 22\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059313} {:answer/id #uuid "024ee0a8-81d1-5cf5-88b6-d174054fe95b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059314} {:answer/id #uuid "0cb34a7e-fbec-5611-b9f0-1ee391be7f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -11 & -7 \\\\ 9 & 34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059315}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c87f3345-8202-5bf7-acde-2b4ceb74f385" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059310}] :question/id #uuid "ea75b5a7-9da3-5be1-8c64-31ab48a8aa3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9681" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060458 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2e2a7fa-1a07-507e-9cfb-d555fed4d92f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059371} {:answer/id #uuid "413612e5-67ec-5bfe-a7b4-1ae63f30a529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -7 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059372} {:answer/id #uuid "4c1f7f26-d02f-5e3f-a75e-088281efd141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059373} {:answer/id #uuid "4f81fba0-53c1-5618-97a3-e5a601c25bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059374} {:answer/id #uuid "4fa3e0c4-2a51-5f34-aca2-36798ca2ba7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059375}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0e2f5d0b-4478-5dc8-803a-bd9eeb731d12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059370}] :question/id #uuid "86bd8759-9672-5297-874b-c9bf15a86252" :question/math-academy-id "q-9965" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A) = 5$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "037393f2-b6d0-5f15-83d8-ecc1860d366c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238112} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab2f7b0-2737-5b4c-bbd9-35ee06e4f051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238979} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0bd746-222a-5820-82fc-3ca96f0e2566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239002} {:answer/id #uuid "d9eb1982-ea08-5419-a703-c8a1cd07e7c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239957} {:answer/id #uuid "ff00e538-8c1b-580a-b72d-811689b8542b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239002} :answer-field/id #uuid "703ead68-58ab-5b1c-a34a-4f9cab386dc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240537}] :question/id #uuid "0b281857-5cf5-5dda-b8cb-bae31f90bde6" :question/math-academy-id "q-104134" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4f2334d-4d19-5657-ae3e-4861480ed63d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298594} :answer-field/id #uuid "78b9513e-697d-5d7b-bee1-be7a3d121ec8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299048} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbfc66b-fff8-5004-b6dd-86427e259c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297674} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d77a70-66b2-5ffc-82b6-2ce4bec2f8bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90e59730-fbc2-5bbb-83ce-1f84517628d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298183} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9818ff9-bf1d-504a-a640-f403039467ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299378}] :question/id #uuid "0876fd99-09ab-5402-abb3-c07e19b050b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-319360" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-5.$\n\n|  |  | $-17$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $12$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n|  |  | $-3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & -12 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b1e8767-de2d-52c7-8e2b-c1d59dee9c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298230} :answer-field/id #uuid "083d9e98-ca8d-5676-958b-ffeedf627de1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1899ba9d-d3c7-55ce-9eb0-e8c2dc7a4673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297659} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e3ce860-5116-5e9b-8117-529c03e68d73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298901} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5975fdb6-cb9e-539a-b015-6e5266540e3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297926} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b9f6c6-8575-50de-8fb6-95b3ce4f2904" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299478}] :question/id #uuid "228d219f-a988-51e3-add6-8253de28fd6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-319370" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-4.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\,$ |  | $4$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |\n|  |  | $7$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a46a2082-4701-5caa-8a18-53b0c4269a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298274} :answer-field/id #uuid "598ac1fb-ed3b-5180-8cb1-1204c40529bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66ae1504-4970-5613-87dc-94b7c840f849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297990} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e4160be-bab1-5130-a5b3-baad952ec2d9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd4225cd-a6f9-5811-a080-99edbbbc07c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298445} :answer-field/id #uuid "b02672dc-f7e5-58dc-a2a8-072fe03a302b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299233}] :question/id #uuid "74394102-8729-5a30-8d7e-62d8f0117047" :question/math-academy-id "q-319372" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=7.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\,$ |  | $-11$ | {{field-2}} | $3$ |  |\n|  |  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -11 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aca02af-1267-5495-8514-3c0b3c60eb1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298229} :answer-field/id #uuid "334b73ec-67fc-5e0a-a799-7aa8a5b37cd6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43320049-f27b-50cd-97bc-171b22e5c4c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297824} :answer-field/id #uuid "78f99d59-45ab-5371-902e-8352a898486d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e895a78-e9aa-58ba-aab5-2fa17cb12e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297950} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b9d8fad-aa30-5871-84b3-b6f919b19455" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49aed189-4a5b-58cc-bc59-cee854ce956e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297854} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ece9237-745d-5b97-a4df-453863812eaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299163}] :question/id #uuid "ca1a8117-1d26-5acd-beac-beb6e4c1cfa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-319395" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | $-3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ {{field-2}} |  | $-1$ | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)(2-3)-0(\\,-2-(-3)\\,)+(-3+3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "742aed52-3923-5d3e-aae7-5ca575086d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361349} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad587c3-4f5c-5eca-b96d-64e234660df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361450} {:answer/id #uuid "a4c8cb0e-1acd-5b83-85e0-b9b1a7bde4b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361575} {:answer/id #uuid "caa1fb09-e645-5bb3-bc36-d3b843dcd6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361752} {:answer/id #uuid "e206a94e-4884-53b0-b2c6-1a2394ba3c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361575} :answer-field/id #uuid "240210d3-d2e3-5a83-9c97-d93c03a1d0de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362012}] :question/id #uuid "7e033a7c-c230-5700-a5b4-d8c955024d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-9967" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & =4\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386055 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e5a90ce-5f43-5f35-b7b8-583244a42439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386057} {:answer/id #uuid "8602540d-4801-5042-9916-98e607f58c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386058} {:answer/id #uuid "c57393fc-dedc-5a9b-9994-032d00d28eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386059} {:answer/id #uuid "8bc9fb87-d9dc-5a6b-ab93-485448959e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386060} {:answer/id #uuid "66812ddb-563d-5415-bd8f-27772bb7e151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386060} :answer-field/id #uuid "e416161a-9bd1-5b5b-810d-ebf9a09026af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386056}] :question/id #uuid "852dcdfe-ad8b-55fc-ab02-b3cb773c55c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-103533" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f6f82c2-90c5-5b86-9116-e45789f5346b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 18 \\\\ -12 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393294} {:answer/id #uuid "48104ce2-f01f-520d-9994-ff0f604fb955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -18 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393295} {:answer/id #uuid "e267455a-8414-553e-ad9e-957e9a3d2a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393296} {:answer/id #uuid "792ada25-1920-5890-a2c7-80e2010138b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393297} {:answer/id #uuid "1506d6fc-6064-5295-a81e-822db7a19957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393298} :answer-field/id #uuid "14ebbec9-43d1-5641-a2c2-12f7a04b7202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393293}] :question/id #uuid "2d1042ad-eb6e-59f8-9dab-abab5265f662" :question/math-academy-id "q-73485" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=12.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & -18 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 18 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16cc7665-faef-5318-96fb-c89a1b7adc64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426296} {:answer/id #uuid "39a3852a-5680-51e4-9e2a-405e8aa0a909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426298} {:answer/id #uuid "95310ad0-4ea0-549a-b41e-47e2e1481ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426301} {:answer/id #uuid "b9fbec83-d0b7-55ad-a7b0-15c8c1d2d21d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426302} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2f21f0-c001-5a27-883c-872065513e5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426298} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b1f25d6-5390-5fe3-998f-b7a40d9649c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426306}] :question/id #uuid "ccf4f432-0d42-54bc-b36a-bd39fd754033" :question/math-academy-id "q-73478" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Using the Matrix of Cofactors"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059755 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059564 :question/id #uuid "9180ff3b-46d2-5df7-81b6-ac75bef51e00" :question/math-academy-id "e-4515" :question/problem "The entry $a'_{31}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n![](images/4b/4b816f3bc511cd6170658d9b75715fc6385feeea1e768cd44d1bd199b67bf853.svg) \nequals $1$. Find the value of $k$." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & k \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(3k-0)-2(-6-0)-2(6+k) \\\\  & =9k+12-12-2k \\\\  & =7k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry $a'_{31}$ in $A^{-1},$ we need to know the value of $c_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & k \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & k \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since $A^{-1}=\\dfrac{1}{\\det (A)}C^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7k}\\cdot (6+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{6+k}{7k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that $a'_{31}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6+k}{7k} & =1 \\\\ 6+k & =7k \\\\ 6 & =6k \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0315a0c1-8e93-55c4-b28a-30f0ae9610cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357784} {:answer/id #uuid "77c1dc2e-024e-5c4b-beb2-f733502ac77d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358787} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff9ce2a-cbe8-5d79-93a4-76f40fb9e37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358869} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4d33c6-a100-512f-a9be-112dbf385d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358957} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d1af3f-8416-5b82-9e39-9309a5040a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358869} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d9ac11a-04f8-5372-b25f-a5363dbf63f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360021}] :question/id #uuid "20571cf0-076d-5c7b-a788-d7a5f5cb703e" :question/math-academy-id "q-9710" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ k & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $18.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ k & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ k & 0\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-24)-2(0-4k)+3(0-k) \\\\  & =8k-3k-24 \\\\  & =5k-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-18) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5k-24}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{5k-24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=18$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{18}{5k-24} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5k-24} & =1 \\\\ 1 & =5k-24 \\\\ 25 & =5k \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060459 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e65ae8a-57ce-5eb7-8254-bbe131d8f40c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059377} {:answer/id #uuid "b31705b8-2e69-5452-b12a-9cd85d22b26a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059378} {:answer/id #uuid "ff8b60ca-2038-56d9-bf33-2d7df3d1d28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059379} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2241db-dca5-5b98-b283-c76148dd792e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059380} {:answer/id #uuid "58134502-f6c0-5d83-9274-d6f7f28fca66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059381}] :answer-field/id #uuid "168f3dd3-003b-54d0-ae3c-e643ac553095" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059376}] :question/id #uuid "c04effc9-bb43-5aa7-be8b-3e036c90cdc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-9997" :question/problem "The entry $a_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & k & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $-1$ and $det(A) = 4 - 4k$. Find the value of $k$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0823e679-5623-5513-8197-33a1c8ae8c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238141} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef0a0c8-e834-5d68-a259-7fedd6fed2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238732} {:answer/id #uuid "6c5fede8-1aad-5729-9d8a-208e730ea058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238989} {:answer/id #uuid "e74baa48-26f8-5695-bad5-d271d1e3e38f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240091} {:answer/id #uuid "fa084b2e-50e1-5131-aea7-50c9409524aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238732} :answer-field/id #uuid "65817036-87eb-5cc8-80d8-f7e75f7b7758" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240517}] :question/id #uuid "57a186fd-b1ba-539f-bb9d-e1998b570fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-104428" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=2k+2.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2k+2\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2k+2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k+1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k+1 & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3541fac5-1091-5ae2-a5ad-314c1f884760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238516} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae53416-c44d-546d-8f7e-7708603910aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238842} {:answer/id #uuid "6328ad49-14be-5303-988b-aaee411b7a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238926} {:answer/id #uuid "eb9f65d2-628a-5c01-b36e-b3ccb0b68a33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240128} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a8d1a8-0d2d-581e-9482-a9f728baa3e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240216} :answer-field/id #uuid "57747a39-2687-5194-90fc-e0d6b4a69104" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240491}] :question/id #uuid "539f41b1-227f-56ae-b693-cf3443bf466c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104431" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $-1$ and $det(A)=4-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=4-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-2k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =2-k \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3907885c-b8d9-5a8a-b101-b8bacd3c100c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238548} {:answer/id #uuid "59dc3dbc-a563-5ed7-a2b8-0b53ab3690df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238829} {:answer/id #uuid "7219f929-3c4c-5130-ba67-06b6ec68f6bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239034} {:answer/id #uuid "e1294134-a47b-51be-972a-dbe70aba54ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240033} {:answer/id #uuid "e666f6f4-3b9a-508e-addb-22f8d57a69de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238548} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d4629b7-d427-5661-a6f1-3af0b7b88fc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240464}] :question/id #uuid "55417378-dec5-552f-8b04-ebd15181a9f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104439" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=k-4.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-4\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{22}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{22} & =(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{22}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{22} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{22}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{k-4} \\\\ k-4 & =-4 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0032ffbe-ef0e-59aa-b26f-1bbc10e77544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290634} :answer-field/id #uuid "84f92a9c-0b0f-5450-99ed-3b1e0df3d706" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292148}] :question/id #uuid "5a90f7ea-2f5b-53dd-b349-fa9148f654dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-275756" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=-k.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-k)}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dd1446d-3318-52d7-b8ca-ff5fb69db2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291032} :answer-field/id #uuid "e08c8940-8a05-58bf-bed8-cc4535359cbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292434}] :question/id #uuid "3b033d4e-fbed-55f2-bf1a-00675137d39e" :question/math-academy-id "q-275757" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2+k)-(-4+2)-(2k+2) \\\\  & =2+k+2-2k-2 \\\\  & =2-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ -1\\cdot (k-2) & =2 \\\\ k-2 & =-2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a25d310-05ab-55e4-a1c5-609bfd85c0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297780} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a79b5b0-3b96-5509-bde8-4a7499f7d418" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298732}] :question/id #uuid "b74699a3-68fd-5996-962f-7d078766e370" :question/math-academy-id "q-319434" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $\\frac{1}{3}$ and $det(A)=1-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=1-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1\\cdot k-0\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1-2k)}\\cdot (-k) \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{3}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3k & =2k-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6821836-cff5-597c-bfe8-284e273211b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298473} :answer-field/id #uuid "5334a997-fbd8-5492-a178-58a2c8133561" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298918}] :question/id #uuid "d4e42e14-a47f-5067-a3e2-ccca26a8935c" :question/math-academy-id "q-319437" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-1\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-1+2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-1}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{k-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{k-1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k-1 & =-2 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19779c74-033c-527e-8527-75fcd9cd52be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297661} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a13f4b6-0d0b-5ddd-bc05-cb3e7f407353" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299101}] :question/id #uuid "f7cdf079-0dbd-550b-985e-14ed1ec133fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-319442" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=-2k-3.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2k-3\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1+2) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2k-3)}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\,2k+3\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\,2k+3\\,} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 12 & =2k+3 \\\\ 2k & =9 \\\\ k & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9efe1417-3245-50a4-a08e-1226edd401f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298255} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2fd473d-2b44-5cd3-afbc-189ab115bc74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299452}] :question/id #uuid "24df41a5-9c85-5f3d-b3b0-277ec8e095a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-319443" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-2\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(k-2)}\\cdot (k+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2(k+2) & =-(k-2) \\\\ 2k+4 & =-k+2 \\\\ 3k & =-2 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299801 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f879e289-265f-50e1-93a8-bc1f3228e612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298611} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a8d0a5-264a-526a-bf26-7c2ead18114a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298984}] :question/id #uuid "dc09a39f-9bc3-5b8d-97b8-ec01ec4b162d" :question/math-academy-id "q-319859" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\,(0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot k)+(-1)\\,(0\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =(2+1)-2\\,(-k)+(-1)\\,(-k) \\\\  & =3+2k+k \\\\  & =3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-(4-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3k+3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3k+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3}{3k+3} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3k-3 & =-6 \\\\ -3k & =-6+3 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{-3} \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbeaf4d4-0e00-520e-99d0-3bee5b93deca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298438} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcfa3e0a-bb95-5124-94ff-faa0c2a5654f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299384}] :question/id #uuid "7aba959b-00b2-5aea-a09a-80fa0c6d7e58" :question/math-academy-id "q-319937" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot k)+(0\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+(0\\cdot k-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =2(k-2)+3-3 \\\\  & =2k-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2k-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =-(k-2) \\\\ k-2 & =-1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f85809-939f-5696-b20f-6a24d1b3a8b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297553} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c533b51-00bb-5918-948d-af70d14f79e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298739}] :question/id #uuid "44f3f3e2-3340-514f-8bf3-b71afd4ac18e" :question/math-academy-id "q-319944" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ k & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nequals $-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ k & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ k & -1\\end{aligned}|+(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)((-1)(-1)-(-2)(-2))+2((-2)(-1)-(-2)k)+(-2)((-2)(-2)-(-1)k) \\\\  & =(-2)(1-4)+2(2+2k)+(-2)(4+k) \\\\  & =6+4+4k-8-2k \\\\  & =2k+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-((-2)(-2)-(-2)k) \\\\  & =-(4+2k) \\\\  & =-2k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2k-4}{2k+2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k+2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=-2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k+2}{k+1} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{k+2}{k+1} & =2 \\\\ k+2 & =2k+2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "444cd60d-98f8-57c7-9875-93fe9bccf0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339729} {:answer/id #uuid "534e79d6-1a48-52d9-8361-6b5e12a9cdf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339897} {:answer/id #uuid "53b60466-c23f-5e4c-9676-8a33e27c13b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339902} {:answer/id #uuid "87d00cf2-3923-56f4-a41d-5b87aa3fb375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340345} {:answer/id #uuid "da2aff30-bbeb-5d42-9525-3fe5517ebd88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341064} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ff8668-6658-5885-8426-f8efdc154b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341502}] :question/id #uuid "4a069e33-ab79-5e52-8347-ee8dc3251c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-73535" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=6+3k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=6+3k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2-(-1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6+3k}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{33}^{′}=\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{2+k} \\\\ 2+k & =4 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "665c812a-56dd-5bc5-b0c8-ffde25e8fa1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340028} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5fface-39c3-5bf8-a1ce-22c8363e23e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340717} {:answer/id #uuid "b15c3399-c900-542c-998e-a75077eccf14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340742} {:answer/id #uuid "c27c70d1-a640-5ece-ae8a-27b55a8741af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340859} {:answer/id #uuid "e7fa4eea-3361-5d16-9459-3c3594fb683d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340028} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa240fd-e96d-535e-8b4a-f32a7de1ce5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341453}] :question/id #uuid "33a7f588-04f8-5fc0-9705-3e73eb1453a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73542" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-0)+(-2k-0)+0 \\\\  & =-2k-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1-(-3)) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k+1} & =1 \\\\ 2 & =k+1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05beee91-a392-5f65-88d2-f7fc95e409b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339177} {:answer/id #uuid "817291a6-cca7-53a6-bdbd-a95cc30beb48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340293} {:answer/id #uuid "98547d62-efa4-543b-b561-835c71d9986d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340498} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1fa043-012b-58dc-8eb3-9d118befac20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340804} {:answer/id #uuid "e51c2424-ac45-594a-b4be-5f0fea419df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341155} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c974da0-7d8a-5c4f-9610-badc09e2e785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341544}] :question/id #uuid "93b0be09-4ca6-5085-9855-e90445a7accc" :question/math-academy-id "q-73545" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{11}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $\\frac{4}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-k-6)-(0-3) \\\\  & =-2k-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{11}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{11}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{11} & =(-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-k-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{11} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-9}\\cdot (-k-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{k+6}{2k+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{11}^{′}=\\frac{4}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+6}{2k+9} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 5(k+6) & =4(2k+9) \\\\ 5k+30 & =8k+36 \\\\ 3k & =-6 \\\\ k & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362389 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bfe9eb7-0858-52db-9dfb-831c6cfdd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361032} {:answer/id #uuid "92da08bc-b94a-5969-b999-e830f9be45bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361489} {:answer/id #uuid "d820da19-1020-5cd4-ad52-3b72b70b868e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361798} {:answer/id #uuid "dda5046b-7496-5105-85c6-0e609a2a6b0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361825} {:answer/id #uuid "e3499b31-131f-5fed-9b53-def82bb10a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361854} :answer-field/id #uuid "7631dea4-74c6-5439-9236-5c814d4472e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362080}] :question/id #uuid "3e095599-c87c-5424-992d-faffcd2cd697" :question/math-academy-id "q-9980" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $\\frac{2}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(k-2)-3(4-6)+1(4-3k) \\\\  & =2k-4+6+4-3k \\\\  & =6-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-k}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6-k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{2}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{6-k} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2\\cdot 5 & =2(6-k) \\\\ 10 & =12-2k \\\\ 2k & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "360fced2-8218-5819-b49f-a6bdb1fc1bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361080} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5a24fa-708c-583a-a345-c52f3aa911d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361533} {:answer/id #uuid "b26d0910-a34a-5209-9a33-b42495f6695f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361628} {:answer/id #uuid "c9642213-619d-5f39-b7b7-a194e5db904f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361747} {:answer/id #uuid "e3588d61-9553-531b-9d36-cee636d25f26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361855} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec73497-ac99-5d21-88bb-baefe07c1bbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361992}] :question/id #uuid "90452d65-c7b3-548e-83d9-2c700d6e9c0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-9998" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2(2k-0)+2(k-0) \\\\  & =-4k+2k \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-2) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k} & =-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5a77823-c6b0-5dfd-b080-ffe4cfc11f5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382258} {:answer/id #uuid "a381d779-2e85-5aaf-8b89-c41349f150fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382259} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb7cd1d-1fab-5c3b-9461-a541a4c58031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382260} {:answer/id #uuid "f9757233-a669-5535-91c9-3301d2cdc860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382261} {:answer/id #uuid "af3bcfe1-d593-5fe7-88cf-00c2b3af0a03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382261} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf58cd3e-d1ca-5107-be49-843e76215f44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382257}] :question/id #uuid "53b328c9-6698-53f6-9c7d-d6d44c5e77f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73533" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $\\frac{1}{18}$ and $det(A)=-18.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-18\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ k & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ k & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}\\cdot (2+k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{18}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{18}(2+k) & =\\frac{1}{18} \\\\ 2+k & =-1 \\\\ k & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "332694ea-bd99-5523-b1d8-48a224b3dc34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426297} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed8db16-e8bd-5c83-b560-aef74fb47014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426299} {:answer/id #uuid "864823ca-9fd6-5647-872e-3574bd6be0c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426300} {:answer/id #uuid "d90a60bf-c9df-5642-a65f-043b1fbac549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426303} {:answer/id #uuid "f712f3e2-029b-5a8a-b19e-340bb36a3186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426300} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ea44ec1-58ba-5956-a980-aec4c772ced8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426307}] :question/id #uuid "60094f6c-d2bd-58df-8627-15176f255263" :question/math-academy-id "q-104435" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nequals $2.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-k-6)-0+1(6-k) \\\\  & =-k-6+6-k \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-2-2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{k} & =2 \\\\ -2 & =2k \\\\ -\\frac{2}{2} & =k \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cofactor Method To Solve for an Unknown Quantity"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059756 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059565 :question/id #uuid "26e9a55f-7711-5d8f-ab0a-e8638f2d2dec" :question/math-academy-id "e-4516" :question/problem "Determine the entry $a'_{23}$ in the inverse of the matrix ![](images/96/967f00655054db75990de13f3634f8d0b320ffde849057ce8cc9a19c58754aa2.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(2-0)-3(0-0)-3(0-1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry $a'_{23}$ in $A^{-1},$ we need to know the value of $c_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}{M}_{32} \\\\  & =(-1)^{5}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1\\cdot (0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since $A^{-1}=\\dfrac{1}{\\det (A)}C^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\na'_{23} = \\dfrac{1}{-1}c_{32} = -1\\cdot 0 = 0.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f06230e-8816-51ce-b392-2abd455f3b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285208} {:answer/id #uuid "4e8539bc-f4a1-50db-90f6-0b45e3ceff04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285517} {:answer/id #uuid "52f9a129-aa6f-59fe-9748-78c62d9d1a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285550} {:answer/id #uuid "d79adfbb-4209-5e76-80b7-c3a2f369dbcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286751} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b8e647-e565-5c04-9e76-013451742246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285517} :answer-field/id #uuid "cec0d804-b8fa-5b33-8525-d5694c64c34d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287572}] :question/id #uuid "ce77ea41-d1eb-55f8-914d-e1a94a42a6b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-18279" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(6-0)+2(0+1)+4(0+3) \\\\  & =6+2+12 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-4-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7576155e-753f-578e-a4ec-c1e146863345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285876} {:answer/id #uuid "7804ba9f-5287-5069-b31b-fbfc92859355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285906} {:answer/id #uuid "94a9a448-efa8-5e13-8fb2-e9929ad565e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286140} {:answer/id #uuid "e6986340-6e6f-5163-a46c-b7ce43a43001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286898} {:answer/id #uuid "ff4f3922-637f-578e-9c1d-529afc788b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285906} :answer-field/id #uuid "00f3d5af-0a6c-5449-9acd-f6ef2a68a144" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287139}] :question/id #uuid "882c4c5b-7c6a-5276-989d-a6c4749ae87b" :question/math-academy-id "q-18280" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =5|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(0-2)+0+3(-2+3) \\\\  & =-10+0+3 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-15-0 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33}=\\frac{1}{-7}\\cdot (-15)=\\frac{15}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240871 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "318e4ff1-9eda-5227-97de-069fe65726f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238485} {:answer/id #uuid "581fb52d-c562-5a61-83a7-0ccc875e2d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238814} {:answer/id #uuid "852c2a15-9bb2-5c2f-a3f3-70dc20643dc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239213} {:answer/id #uuid "99946c30-ae52-50d2-ab9b-73478b6df019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239388} {:answer/id #uuid "c135f6ba-7057-5a82-9972-767caa7e7342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239388} :answer-field/id #uuid "05ee2e28-0127-5de7-9d19-9359e9043495" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240334}] :question/id #uuid "fc11b8c2-85be-59ad-bbca-214a365781c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-104413" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(1-0)-0+(-1-0) \\\\  & =3+0-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "321b8d3b-cd54-5aec-b3c6-614d9119d85e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238490} {:answer/id #uuid "82f83531-f2a4-50ef-b8cf-747f2110b4e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239195} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a62450-4a64-5b83-97a1-956b91c29de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239765} {:answer/id #uuid "c3910286-f59a-54dd-9194-1920e9c24f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239783} {:answer/id #uuid "efe95074-4ae4-5190-923c-417bab521d7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239765} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c312751-eff3-5874-b792-a6fa94261128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240346}] :question/id #uuid "d6189c9e-c299-5fe1-934e-c85b7854108f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104416" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2+1)-(1-2)+0 \\\\  & =-3+1+0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1-4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-5)=\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45901bed-283a-5f6b-a0e8-c82fb99c77cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285423} {:answer/id #uuid "590cea1c-0a7c-5f07-8068-694058c3a868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285603} {:answer/id #uuid "6649b745-668c-5e5d-b83b-1cf253b1e095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285716} {:answer/id #uuid "d89e0dd4-5791-5cf7-b3cb-314c7f78a09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286760} {:answer/id #uuid "e7904946-6db5-50df-9602-9962763b4fcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285716} :answer-field/id #uuid "70430d88-1fa4-5196-ac2c-0e31afc80076" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287382}] :question/id #uuid "dc94d59e-a3d1-5387-8338-9ada65b5d11f" :question/math-academy-id "q-18281" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(0+9)-4(0-6)+1(0+2) \\\\  & =18+24+2 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-6) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}=\\frac{1}{44}\\cdot 6=\\frac{3}{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14576e31-28a0-51c9-98e0-cb0e88b08edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284968} {:answer/id #uuid "87d3e443-ddd4-51ad-bc3b-642891265441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286034} {:answer/id #uuid "a41b5f85-604a-5b3f-adf2-0829d0c2aa47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286292} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e84826-763e-57fb-8b0f-9e77c3cef0a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :an