er/id #uuid "11d094be-9dc7-5405-8cce-9907e9c51654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284945} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9cbbbd-12e1-5cce-8786-a3ceed193971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285356} {:answer/id #uuid "ab1a2f27-2e9e-5b7f-a874-29bebc8a2d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286347} {:answer/id #uuid "b72dc0b0-3001-5783-b493-cbb1bcd44dc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284836} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c45b83d-dd3d-58f3-83e0-2b583f24f687" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287206}] :question/id #uuid "35c43087-68b2-5ef3-b590-6196109cdd18" :question/math-academy-id "q-18287" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ if its determinant is $24.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =24-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}=\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot 24=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aba01f9-7f51-5a8f-a7a8-dc4fa8fb483a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285161} {:answer/id #uuid "51897cf6-89ff-547a-a77d-fb4c229f6e36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285537} {:answer/id #uuid "83757217-5865-5baa-8ad8-1b2c54dde4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285995} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f44981-7ac4-5b60-aa71-18f4807ae1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286563} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e75515-8616-5fe3-a6a1-8dc2e1fa3a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{71}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286563} :answer-field/id #uuid "909dfb56-2abf-58f1-9f5d-3fcdb81ce8b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287447}] :question/id #uuid "b862f7e3-dfeb-537e-b5d6-1de6a752faf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-18288" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ if its determinant is $71.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-3-10) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}=\\frac{1}{71}\\cdot 13=\\frac{13}{71}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292885 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ed7a213-aacc-56d2-9779-25fff16d3e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290969} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7851796-9230-52fb-8a26-b3ea3a329032" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292298}] :question/id #uuid "30ba35b5-5f35-540d-9096-c30d7199aaa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-275755" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2+2)-0-3(2-0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(6-0) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299754 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6598caed-bd43-5485-82fc-6172d6afee81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297986} :answer-field/id #uuid "87b160ba-8853-58cf-97da-7d8ad0eb9b07" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299093}] :question/id #uuid "e7e72b45-0695-5b36-9476-7542514f8aaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-319409" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-3-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4ed675a-e374-5734-95e6-b38d1d46a8c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298339} :answer-field/id #uuid "9144a26f-d207-5329-a4f2-7e4b73ff0242" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299117}] :question/id #uuid "e9cc9cf4-3e2c-5fa2-9cc3-9a41fb5db658" :question/math-academy-id "q-319413" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-2-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299757 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08bb5b15-8035-5a87-b994-7a63a290fd15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5/13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5/13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297598} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a8cea55-04b6-5a91-988e-863b5a98418a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298947}] :question/id #uuid "8dd1f6d6-3609-5dae-86b5-57186f677ef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-319416" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(2-(-3))+2(4-0)+0(6-0) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}^{t}={c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1+4) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3eaad9-1dc3-55cb-ab62-7139f24f233d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298432} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef19aba-acb5-5246-8048-25a4732b0153" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299494}] :question/id #uuid "d6120ca6-9e08-5dd7-8756-664c0b14c937" :question/math-academy-id "q-319420" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n${a}_{31}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(2+1)-0\\,(0-1)+2\\,(-0-2) \\\\  & =3-0-4 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}^{t}={c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67507fa1-9c8b-533b-b35f-b2b75970e742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297996} :answer-field/id #uuid "86f29c10-686e-51f4-8830-5217f4abdf63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299089}] :question/id #uuid "2b5cf762-3178-5e63-a1b0-8da0e65dccf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-319546" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $17.$\n\n${a}_{13}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30fc4049-b346-5ef3-b721-8b7b6804b08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297759} :answer-field/id #uuid "83e9901e-f892-512e-a362-56ac30375949" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299083}] :question/id #uuid "66b7eb82-0c6f-5154-a5bd-434c9571ba55" :question/math-academy-id "q-319549" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $3.$\n\n${a}_{21}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\,(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c573351-ee99-56f5-889f-894b79759197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298090} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e78f910-eafd-5dde-95e7-840e8bbf0359" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298904}] :question/id #uuid "959ebdb0-727b-5193-9194-4f73c8f717da" :question/math-academy-id "q-319550" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $-22.$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-22}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Element of the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :topic/math-academy-id 154 :topic/title "Calculating the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Using the Cofactor Method"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060649} :activity/id #uuid "b3e816b9-b26c-5877-ab1b-44486bb0568d" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060649 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060931 :tutorial/content "The **determinant** of a general $2 \\times 2$ matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}$\nis denoted $\\text {det} ({A})$ and computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, given the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ \nthe determinant is\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = {\\color{blue}{2}} \\cdot {\\color{blue}{3}} - {\\color{red}{1}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{5}} = 1.\n$$\n\nTo remember how to compute the determinant of a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, you can imagine taking the product of the diagonal of the matrix, and then subtracting the product of the off-diagonal terms, as follows:\n\n![](images/25/2594f99e0f02241dc6d01f85c82923103df1d6fb4dda5ca03d438637f5178a28.png)\n\nLater, we will see that the determinant is related to the \"volume\" spanned by the row vectors or column vectors in a matrix. We will also see that the determinant can tell us about many other properties of a matrix. \n\nHowever, in this lesson, we will just focus on computing the determinant." :tutorial/id #uuid "e436044e-13ed-56ec-aac0-2ed10a498cf3" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3012 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "66d8d225-b76d-563f-9d07-02583faa8c02" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060650}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060650 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2129aee3-923d-57de-8bdc-983ffdf787f1"} :step/id #uuid "ab1798dd-58dd-5284-95e3-80bff9567ac0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060651}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060651 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26e8a6ff-e5ed-59a7-b31d-1981495bf26a"} :step/id #uuid "fea3cd81-2d56-54b3-86bc-084fbde4e754" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060652}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060652 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccdde46-a4ab-517e-910b-571a3a166b6a"} :step/id #uuid "805274da-e280-5f9d-bdf5-86aef1a31364"}] :activity/title "The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059885}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186049044 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059748 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059557 :question/id #uuid "2b6e8845-a53d-510c-b44f-1b00271ee507" :question/math-academy-id "e-4434" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =18-10 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2129aee3-923d-57de-8bdc-983ffdf787f1" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510622 :question-generator/id #uuid "53947596-3d55-5413-bf29-25cec1927b42" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186059748.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bef9d71-e6eb-54e4-8e8e-a529aa8f1992" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241284} {:answer/id #uuid "af58227c-7285-5719-b8ee-6e95dc121818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242708} {:answer/id #uuid "b33e532a-b90d-5de2-812f-858d1ea4ce57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242741} {:answer/id #uuid "b7782812-7471-5927-8799-42fa4e8f2c90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242786} {:answer/id #uuid "d690db23-f51d-5c54-a3fe-07d2f24b9b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241284} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd1e424-be57-57db-8709-ae267fc7b54a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243770}] :question/id #uuid "67459f8a-4276-51e0-8ff0-10c56a6d248e" :question/math-academy-id "q-1079" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{det}(A)$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-6 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adeef685-13ff-59be-8555-fa285a4b673e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056359} {:answer/id #uuid "e93e332c-0067-5a8e-978e-451498a19a05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056360} {:answer/id #uuid "09a86a42-c0b8-57e0-a93a-e191a7d6b5f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056361} {:answer/id #uuid "0a801cc5-5312-593f-9422-e650a8b22f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056362} {:answer/id #uuid "3f33f5eb-9069-5dcd-955b-ccc0b698801b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056363}] :answer-field/id #uuid "809ecc7b-96f9-5877-beda-07f945eee167" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056358}] :question/id #uuid "ea87b1ac-4625-5a01-8d70-68a1975a00a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-11648" :question/problem "What is $\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{vmatrix}$?"}