& {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| & =3\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x})-{z}^{2}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =-3x-2y{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245f8b76-960f-5227-85be-1848c57026fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(ru-st)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333328} {:answer/id #uuid "5179db59-ecf5-527f-b152-14da85049ace" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6ru-3st" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333736} {:answer/id #uuid "925c8e43-d240-576e-96a7-f6450bcebaff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(st-ru)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334293} {:answer/id #uuid "be3cb9cd-cb94-5657-98ff-b3d91e1ff9d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6ru+3st" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334635} {:answer/id #uuid "fa49eaa1-621e-5ca8-a141-b55927a350aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(2st-ru)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(st-ru)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334293} :answer-field/id #uuid "8926dc70-416f-5104-b768-f00f2078937e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335501}] :question/id #uuid "3f8c0050-79c4-5426-9e5c-a8628ebc0ae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-69650" :question/problem "Calculate $det(H)$, if\n    $H=\\begin{bmatrix}-2r & 3s \\\\ -2t & 3u\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(H) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2r & 3s \\\\ -2t & 3u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2r\\cdot 3u-3s\\cdot (-2t) \\\\  & =-6ru-(-6st) \\\\  & =-6ru+6st \\\\  & =6(st-ru)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510569 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a997286f-4db9-53ee-8849-22966e083d6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{113}{280}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{113}{280}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510578} :answer-field/id #uuid "aac06ef3-2984-5073-a683-edc5d64f81a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510579}] :question/id #uuid "107b0d08-c0c2-5e3b-a247-c4238dbd6d8f" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{7})-\\frac{9}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{9}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{45}{56}-(-\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{113}{280}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e54747-95d9-5771-963b-49dcf4295948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510574} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b44817c-904a-519b-9cfd-76497778888f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510570}] :question/id #uuid "295bc951-4997-5df9-ab67-20bc32e8016a" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{7} & -\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{7} & -\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{5})-(-\\frac{9}{5})\\cdot \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}-(-\\frac{9}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{55}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "782fb4f6-27a0-5506-9beb-555ca18e4273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1784}{1323}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1784}{1323}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510577} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2dbf444-3856-5b85-8fac-b9843fa4dd21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510580}] :question/id #uuid "4f9be678-4285-5f11-ba52-fd42fc00b682" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{9} & -\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{9} & -\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot (-\\frac{8}{3})-(-\\frac{4}{7})\\cdot \\frac{2}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{27}-(-\\frac{8}{49}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1784}{1323}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0e44b6c-314a-5501-9b95-06b4d75b5730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{513}{140}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{513}{140}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510581} :answer-field/id #uuid "23459979-cbd9-5238-a961-af2acea3f96e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510571}] :question/id #uuid "554f7f1f-b6ff-5426-9de0-5f0d3de16c53" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{5} & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{5} & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{5}{4})-\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{28}-(-\\frac{21}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{513}{140}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5c3e732-c3bb-5b5f-b786-d49ab1ea186a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{113}{210}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{113}{210}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510582} :answer-field/id #uuid "25acb654-19ec-53d5-9cf7-5fa54e4d05cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510572}] :question/id #uuid "f71665cc-a4c6-5094-b683-7caeca8eef3e" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{7} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{7} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{7}\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{35}-\\frac{5}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{113}{210}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Non-Integer Entries"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059750 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059559 :question/id #uuid "043a5e58-e1a0-50a5-b1be-d404e6262991" :question/math-academy-id "e-4436" :question/problem "If\n${A} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        2 & -1  \\\\\n        -3 & k\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack$\nand\n$\\det({A}) = 5$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot k-(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2k-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=5,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =5 \\\\ 2k-3 & =5 \\\\ 2k & =8 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccdde46-a4ab-517e-910b-571a3a166b6a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0ff914a-1317-5490-ba59-b2437dd6665a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056365} {:answer/id #uuid "be028415-acff-5d6d-8080-1a4b0687fc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k =-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056366} {:answer/id #uuid "28d6cf2e-8b16-58ce-af42-d46cb399a7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k =-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056367} {:answer/id #uuid "3882486c-1efa-5685-9f10-e83963bf1488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056368} {:answer/id #uuid "585ec4a5-edb5-5cf4-907c-653192911ffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056369}] :answer-field/id #uuid "463bd4e4-2bee-5ee4-b6dd-f8a4f765f86b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056364}] :question/id #uuid "cda11aab-d0f1-5aed-9faf-9b4214024dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11651" :question/problem "If\n$C = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & k\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$det(C) = 3$, what is the value of $k$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8f75c6a-39ca-54ce-90b2-d2fed57bce1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057631} {:answer/id #uuid "f1cc6fa4-5d2d-5ef7-8b9e-ca6b2a04a6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057632} {:answer/id #uuid "34efec5a-0267-59a9-a0e8-a8bbc8e3bbc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057633} {:answer/id #uuid "626288b8-1266-5c66-8802-e4279b82a65f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057634} {:answer/id #uuid "65626e08-ea8e-5f2e-a56f-1de07c241265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057635}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb55465-244d-5741-a788-539ef4e5adf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057630}] :question/id #uuid "e1d88843-5476-50c9-8034-3251a4933b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-19801" :question/problem "If\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 + t & 2t \\\\ -3 & 1 - t\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(A) = 10$, what is the value of $t$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233379 :question/id #uuid "ed3ae951-db6d-557c-8a34-9c013751cf9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127614" :question/problem "If\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & 6 \\\\ 2x & x-2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(D)=-32$, what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 6 \\\\ 2x & x-2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (x-2)-6\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-16x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-32$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-32 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-16x & =-32 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-16x+32 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+16 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0209a06e-c872-52c8-83aa-6e78fe082784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250573} {:answer/id #uuid "0e8f8e5e-07ec-513d-8935-253e50a8994b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250679} {:answer/id #uuid "5c767359-7b77-5594-a325-0a9b4ca901af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251315} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8e6d11-24ab-54f4-9302-a197b45ae78f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252504} {:answer/id #uuid "e407a6b3-d6da-578c-aa7b-c0b520a0af0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5bd1bd-eab3-5250-8633-db4827abfabb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252971}] :question/id #uuid "605f5d22-0a36-54b2-9fda-393ada9a651b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11653" :question/problem "If\n    $M=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\text{det}(M)=2$, what is the value of $w?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-w\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nSince $det(M)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =2 \\\\ 6-4w & =2 \\\\ -4w & =2-6 \\\\ -4w & =-4 \\\\ w & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "231d65c4-afe9-5dda-9ec8-8e657ebc2e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260183} {:answer/id #uuid "2cde1f0f-ce43-5b48-8b5f-a4207965af8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260279} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9b7936-2a9f-5fa6-98b8-c2d31209e615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260296} {:answer/id #uuid "6e18de3f-d88f-51e5-8a5a-4c7a07f3003b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260842} {:answer/id #uuid "72f9541a-9495-523a-a73a-4a7b746e235a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260279} :answer-field/id #uuid "469de0af-655e-5c52-99af-6a01835c14fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262246}] :question/id #uuid "eb9b1b8a-cede-5e44-9f81-ee8a71692716" :question/math-academy-id "q-127604" :question/problem "If\n    $U=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-1$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-k+2)-(-5)\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =7k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-1$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-1 \\\\ 7k+6 & =-1 \\\\ 7k & =-1-6 \\\\ 7k & =-7 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "613ae31f-3ed4-522f-b38e-30b725565300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260710} {:answer/id #uuid "6c66b584-1346-57a8-91c6-b84e73a70782" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260826} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccc1966-d22e-5ca2-85e6-62f888a4ebc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261106} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbbb63f-c7de-5798-b663-aa393eb8f406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261850} {:answer/id #uuid "f645c953-47f3-5b1c-9345-c05fb1f18f37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260826} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae8e73c-6de7-5bcc-a8b5-a2c66229f23e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262142}] :question/id #uuid "7bb355a7-6406-51ad-b4a4-0aaf09eca17d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127606" :question/problem "If\n$T=\\begin{bmatrix}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(T)=-4$, what is the value of $v?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot (v+8)-2v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={v}^{2}+4v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(T)=-4$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v+4 & =0 \\\\ (v+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ v & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aab353e-d8a2-5cee-ad8e-75d89f36942f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259969} {:answer/id #uuid "55f69ea5-658f-54da-aab9-eba230208482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260610} {:answer/id #uuid "77bbba7e-5eef-5fde-bf0b-27cf27e274ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260919} {:answer/id #uuid "e35430a5-8bd9-5cd3-a709-f9d32c9a6cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261873} {:answer/id #uuid "f83c7a76-e478-5e97-87ce-06f9facc6cc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260919} :answer-field/id #uuid "481e7819-63cc-5385-bd4b-6641777b91a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262249}] :question/id #uuid "612dd17c-57fb-5f36-b33a-8e40d39733fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-127607" :question/problem "If\n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}r-3 & r \\\\ 3 & r\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(P)=-9$, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =|\\begin{aligned}r-3 & r \\\\ 3 & r\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(r-3)\\cdot r-r\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={r}^{2}-6r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(P)=-9$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r+9 & =0 \\\\ (r-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ r & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d8c86ed-6d17-58e5-80b8-58959792fbea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260000} {:answer/id #uuid "5da2ff79-d5ff-5f94-843d-fd01485931c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260680} {:answer/id #uuid "63782cc1-1e3c-5b15-9b88-3f08b70112ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260732} {:answer/id #uuid "7a8b63ad-24d0-5034-a4cd-e73692e2757c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260943} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f4b75b-8f4c-53c9-98ea-95862842547a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260000} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e8c9907-19d6-5803-bfec-b352898f4520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262266}] :question/id #uuid "4e03a4dd-5246-5c91-8e03-9d7ad64d917d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127608" :question/problem "If\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}5-p & p \\\\ 3 & p\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(B)=1$, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}5-p & p \\\\ 3 & p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5-p)\\cdot p-p\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-{p}^{2}+2p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(B)=1$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p-1 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-2p+1 & =0 \\\\ (p-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262807 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a37c432-ec3a-54fa-a265-be8a73e5b042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260101} {:answer/id #uuid "570d06e5-402c-5a48-aa29-06ffa92a5243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260619} {:answer/id #uuid "76d5eb3b-a067-51ff-b76b-ba5ac4fdd83a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260912} {:answer/id #uuid "bd179fed-e737-5b98-9f59-7194e6703cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261544} {:answer/id #uuid "d688ed58-3493-5fc2-84fe-15f1d55d1e83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{18}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260101} :answer-field/id #uuid "a12a44ba-4364-5ba9-9b64-63befc571bbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262414}] :question/id #uuid "41f9cebe-1261-5298-9d1d-10bd7138212b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127609" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(A)=-27$, what is the value of $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3y\\cdot (y-5)-y\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=-27$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y+27 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "637424aa-e375-5ca5-bc92-9b93538da967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291058} :answer-field/id #uuid "5deef2d0-b2e7-54ab-a3df-7734195f5705" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292019}] :question/id #uuid "6d712990-6aa9-538b-af72-704fc59cbac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-275598" :question/problem "If\n    $C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\text{det}(C)=-14,$ determine the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-k\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(C)=-14$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-14 \\\\ 6-4k & =-14 \\\\ -4k & =-14-6 \\\\ -4k & =-20 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93399e4d-4d85-580e-9e08-c041fa5d5800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291266} :answer-field/id #uuid "339de4a9-ce7b-517d-9496-4255c739b1c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291908}] :question/id #uuid "d673c24b-03d4-55e8-a5fb-605bc1d6c21f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275601" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(A)=7,$ what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+p)(5-p)-(4p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-3p+5p-{p}^{2}-4p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =15-2p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =15-2p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=7$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =7 \\\\ 15-2p & =7 \\\\ -2p & =-8 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7fa1ff0-7dcd-55bd-a8fb-9db3d54aaf17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298479} :answer-field/id #uuid "154b6de9-0d77-5e77-8de1-45bf6ab48913" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298716}] :question/id #uuid "1e3ffcd6-7f26-5f4f-8230-33ae44d7f744" :question/math-academy-id "q-317377" :question/problem "If\n    $D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\text{det}(D)=-11,$ determine the value of $m.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-m\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10-3m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-11 \\\\ 10-3m & =-11 \\\\ -3m & =-21 \\\\ m & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2846b11-7ae8-5649-abfa-db38bcffb861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298524} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf4f818-ea4f-5a3d-9526-388b53c60cf1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299436}] :question/id #uuid "d0f61095-530a-54e2-bb79-353fa0efed39" :question/math-academy-id "q-317382" :question/problem "If\n$U=\\begin{bmatrix}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(U)=-6$, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =|\\begin{aligned}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1+r)\\cdot 4-(2-r)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =4+4r+10-5r \\\\  & =14-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-6 \\\\ 14-r & =-6 \\\\ -r & =-20 \\\\ r & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299602 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cb2781e-f836-5ab8-a7a5-4a709b95dddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298164} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eda0fee-f95d-5630-8031-5abef3969057" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298688}] :question/id #uuid "6e22859c-f056-5995-96a3-08af912796b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-317385" :question/problem "If\n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(S)=25,$ what is the value of $s?$\n\n$s=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+s)(3-s)-2s(-4) \\\\  & =9-{s}^{2}+8s \\\\  & =-{s}^{2}+8s+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s+9 & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s-16 & =0 \\\\ {s}^{2}-8s+16 & =0 \\\\ (s-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ s & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd1c86f-37e4-5b7b-9ec3-6d55d9670cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333244} {:answer/id #uuid "4342bd65-1b39-56fb-b10b-45b1a8deeebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333618} {:answer/id #uuid "982f2c1a-e0ab-57c2-b71f-62ccc2593e9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334339} {:answer/id #uuid "9e476a33-a9f4-5b54-ad86-0d592acad0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334384} {:answer/id #uuid "ab173fd5-9f80-5b1f-9676-76188073a554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334384} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c672b33-f965-56dc-b5e9-ce679a558195" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335509}] :question/id #uuid "66ad3ebb-398d-57e0-be2a-0ce7c08b87a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-69661" :question/problem "If\n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(S)=2$, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1-p)\\cdot 2-(1+p)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2-2p+3+3p \\\\  & =5+p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=2$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =2 \\\\ 5+p & =2 \\\\ p & =2-5 \\\\ p & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :topic/math-academy-id 152 :topic/title "The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097518} :activity/id #uuid "3b059c68-9dd5-5f61-a9e4-d2768be710f4" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097518 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097841 :tutorial/content "Consider a system of linear equations and its respective augmented matrix $M\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/67/673ea82819858b9a46e0e351a8d6f41b069ed039ee0d31a382110f938f7ef72a.svg)\n\nWe can reduce $M$ to row echelon form using the standard Gaussian elimination algorithm. The algorithm that we use is very similar to the case of $2 \\times 2$ systems. \n\nOur goal is to create a descending \"staircase\" of $1$'s with $0$'s below, and we achieve this using elementary row operations. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & -24\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix is now in row echelon form, and we can apply back substitution to solve the original system of equations.\n\n**Note:** The row echelon form of a matrix is *not* unique.  In the previous example, after the second row operation we arrived at\n\n![](images/35/35627a034b30736abb057c01f3251fc047dce780a8cbcf389f8b5c2c2317d766.svg)\n\nThis augmented matrix is already in row echelon form! However, it is always useful to do an extra step and obtain $1$'s along the main diagonal, like we did previously:\n\n![](images/32/32a252e05e299a206f2f3776a2a04419f21726e1f8f542cfd4f328dac3251f21.svg)\n\nHaving $1$'s along the main diagonal makes the final back substitution process a little easier." :tutorial/id #uuid "5d8cb1c1-9e09-560f-83ad-7c8a3d0a78cc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3155 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "54dae6c6-bb01-588b-b012-dc097a5b2c65" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097519}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097519 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097842 :tutorial/content "The **standard Gaussian elimination** for a $3 \\times 3$ system can be described as follows:\n\n- If $a_{11} \\neq 0$ and $a_{11} \\neq 1,$ then we use the row operation $R_1:=R_1/a_{11}.$\n\n- We use first row and the necessary row operations to make the remaining entries of the first column below $a_{11}$ equal to $0.$ Namely, \n\n- if $a_{21} \\neq 0,$ then we use the row operation $R_2:=R_2 + (-a_{21})R_1;$\n\n- if $a_{31} \\neq 0,$ then we use the row operation $R_3:=R_3 + (-a_{31})R_1.$\n\n- If $a_{22} \\neq 1,$ then we use the row operation $R_2:=R_2/a_{22}.$\n\n- We use the second row and the necessary row operation to make the entry below $a_{22}$ equal to $0.$ Namely, \n\n- if $a_{32} \\neq 0,$ then we use the row operation $R_3:=R_3 + (-a_{32})R_2.$\n\n- If $a_{33} \\neq 1,$ then we use the row operation $R_3:=R_3/a_{33}.$\n\n- In some exceptional cases, such as when the element on the diagonal is equal to $0,$ we first need to exchange rows. Then proceed using the same steps as above.\n\nCarrying out the above algorithm will convert the matrix to row echelon form." :tutorial/id #uuid "955c2b9a-3d5f-52c3-b4f3-62541732ffcc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3156 :tutorial/title "General Algorithm"} :step/id #uuid "4f927453-918f-5476-ba92-06cc1a2e3f72" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097520}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097520 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096672 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827"} :step/id #uuid "8c5555a5-f06e-5c31-9de6-ec1aef27abbb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097521}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097521 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096673 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197"} :step/id #uuid "813ae7dd-cdf7-5b02-ad5e-3911c5f08ece"}] :activity/title "Solving 3x3 Systems of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096856}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186049058 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096672 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096459 :question/id #uuid "b77c065c-3821-513c-9376-6e7108074616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4701" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n![](images/b3/b3512e604d6c4246c5582a75360076115c4bd9b6701c42587f318254b1c026a3.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/76/765eafb8a8b60aec9af512eeb666e2e13dbf83b8bc331b6effa75143930b4892.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2) &=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2) &=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096937 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2af7fa69-5175-5f82-abdc-7a83d1c7437a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414020} {:answer/id #uuid "3faa2fb1-77d5-521f-acea-30296fef736c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414021} {:answer/id #uuid "797daa95-425d-5598-93a6-9f8e22458433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,2,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414024} {:answer/id #uuid "a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414027} {:answer/id #uuid "c64960b9-232a-5479-96de-e63c3bb0d15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,2,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414027} :answer-field/id #uuid "145fd237-737e-5055-9883-501b0228a34c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414029}] :question/id #uuid "6f82ff82-f58e-5dd1-b2bf-5cc0bd58f164" :question/math-academy-id "q-10676" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 25\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 25\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=19 \\\\ y+2z &=13 \\\\ z &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(5)=13\\,⟹\\,y=13-10=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=3$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(3)+2(5)=19\\,⟹\\,x=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=6,y=3$, and $z=5.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨6,3,5⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "046f428e-556f-5956-b78b-d2844abad4b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284826} {:answer/id #uuid "babfedb6-0dfd-59fe-83fc-1aade7621c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286487} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a979f3-bf84-5ce4-a382-9675dac8cb9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286562} {:answer/id #uuid "e3dfdeab-6885-5e75-a55d-ac0b26ea713b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286868} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ba7f8a-2143-5951-aadf-be80dd868963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286487} :answer-field/id #uuid "78caa516-f3d8-59a7-8c65-740773cd1cf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287404}] :question/id #uuid "a19bbe50-faec-58bf-b57a-44ae8f766527" :question/math-academy-id "q-20505" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+6z &=5 \\\\ y-10z &=-11 \\\\ 4x+8y+13z &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & -11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{11}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "335c1d28-6ef0-501b-8648-2c0e5914f807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,6,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263444} {:answer/id #uuid "bda33206-a035-53c6-9921-6f6c110c575a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264647} {:answer/id #uuid "f4057cf8-6668-54c9-bf42-88c4d70eac10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265143} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ca4d3b-5b47-5683-9882-c5ab43df0469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265178} {:answer/id #uuid "fda5f85f-ead2-5bc7-84eb-7f79db911497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,6,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265178} :answer-field/id #uuid "eadf5a06-1fa1-5b76-950d-e8ed3be547ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265664}] :question/id #uuid "49125958-677d-58d5-ae65-4f5b3deb04dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-130926" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=-3 \\\\ y-2z &=-2 \\\\ z &=8,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=8$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-2(8)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-2+16=14.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=14$ and $z=8$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(14)+(8)=-3\\,⟹\\,x=17.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=17,y=14$, and $z=8.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨17,14,8⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb4f677-6e20-5d48-8adf-dad8e569076e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=8$ and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285033} {:answer/id #uuid "67b6832b-f7f1-55d1-92dd-f7c48ee15a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=4$ and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285735} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6c5f1f-a44d-56e0-b1b5-4ebcaafd017f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=6$ and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286213} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0477fe-23d0-5b2c-af42-8e02c492ff15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=2$ and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286234} {:answer/id #uuid "bcba1021-c3fa-5be5-90b6-ccdceb2d3943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=5$ and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=2$ and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286234} :answer-field/id #uuid "13c51648-1907-5520-9df6-2d1f4963b562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287184}] :question/id #uuid "76260352-1678-5f91-b36f-3214c8df1e0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-20263" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=6 \\\\ y+z &=5 \\\\ 2x+3y+2z &=14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=6 \\\\ y+z &=5 \\\\ z &=3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=3$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(3)=5\\,⟹\\,y=5-3=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=2$ and $z=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(2)+(3)=6\\,⟹\\,x=6-5=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1,y=2$ and $z=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15719692-f572-52e2-92ef-7c37695a20ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284977} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb9ba6d-8ad5-5004-96ed-80c84894925e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286091} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5c7bb0-6725-548b-b664-64d4ff92c96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286504} {:answer/id #uuid "d6bbdd67-60e8-56e1-96f6-8012386dd066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286742} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e5b59d-43dc-5f6c-8987-626af7040c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286504} :answer-field/id #uuid "28841267-b70d-52db-841b-c4f0d84407a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287232}] :question/id #uuid "e202a5f2-1485-54d2-ad75-6c42b9340de9" :question/math-academy-id "q-20524" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17efca8f-87be-5b95-8922-289fdb1d26ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285001} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4254ad-d231-50fd-9b68-9ebbd2ce5ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285352} {:answer/id #uuid "45a723dd-0ef1-5ec0-b478-73144022c495" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285424} {:answer/id #uuid "75525907-933a-53d6-ae44-4d6d45f4ca9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285870} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf19ccd-17f1-5cf4-8f69-4973c62ab6fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285352} :answer-field/id #uuid "51bb4809-5d86-5a66-b4a7-5e6d674e0405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287329}] :question/id #uuid "a9aba0f5-8a1c-5403-81c5-fd64e80722c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-20533" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=0 \\\\ y+2z &=0 \\\\ x+y+3z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ae6737-5709-5299-9355-f610cf32cf10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-11,y=4$ and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284870} {:answer/id #uuid "38432a32-b421-5cb9-b804-edecfba79df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1,y=4$ and $z=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285312} {:answer/id #uuid "b532826d-782c-5acc-b69d-27c5cf349663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13,y=-4$ and $z=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286436} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb9a50d-a3e7-56d7-b7e0-47332e68cf82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-2,y=4$ and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286806} {:answer/id #uuid "f110becd-084a-5b17-b76a-616cfd4c91b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286999} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b2ad410-5feb-53d6-a57d-187523cf9154" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287438}] :question/id #uuid "00b50258-32a4-58d0-8a62-9857f481b38c" :question/math-academy-id "q-20542" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=-3 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=2 \\\\ 3x+4y+4z &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 17\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=-3 \\\\ y &=5 \\\\ z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=5$ and $z=-6$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+5+2(-6)=-3\\,⟹\\,x-7=-3\\,⟹\\,x=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4,$ $y=5,$ and $z=-6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1c26475-90bd-5e7a-84b3-47ac0bd01588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367937} {:answer/id #uuid "97a92173-cc7b-5847-916b-da911b96d3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367938} {:answer/id #uuid "3f69175b-4c5a-5019-855c-5dd66c050c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367939} {:answer/id #uuid "135066fa-e5ab-531e-823d-7b8a43cfbd6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367940} {:answer/id #uuid "f54d27f3-bd4c-5652-a2f5-cdb2aeecffce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367938} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee53708-7bbe-5275-be3b-4ffaa95c115d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367936}] :question/id #uuid "8557cbac-c9fb-5ae6-8b4f-ab9d7e2cdf03" :question/math-academy-id "q-20515" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=-4 \\\\ 2x+5y+3z &=-10 \\\\ 3x+6y+4z &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e289daf-4c28-5e8b-b06d-9bfb29306c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,-12,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368704} {:answer/id #uuid "de191ec5-6dfc-5619-92ef-3ef733d0d523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-9,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368705} {:answer/id #uuid "22b06387-1b81-5688-bd9a-ca492425a4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,-6,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368706} {:answer/id #uuid "c999c0cc-98fe-58fa-aacd-b8e42f127e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,-3,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368707} {:answer/id #uuid "52fa9cba-0e91-5d16-a4da-3d9fa8b32a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,-15,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,-6,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368706} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e1e8500-0044-5eb8-b6ac-7951b743cc1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368703}] :question/id #uuid "38fec071-dd2c-5be5-8833-47ebc39dc16e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73569" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 12 & 36 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=1 \\\\ y-3z &=-9 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-3(1)=-9\\,⟹\\,y=-6.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-6$ and $z=1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-(-6)+2(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-7,y=-6$, and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-7,-6,1⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf440d3-3fd9-55cc-926d-c8fb116cd60a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390369} {:answer/id #uuid "07658a20-9348-593b-a22c-bfd4aa0d76d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390370} {:answer/id #uuid "43daa5ce-d019-5af0-b38c-6fa388015557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390371} {:answer/id #uuid "ec19f197-25d0-50fa-b873-ca959251ea66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390372} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6061c2-cc6f-52e0-b686-f2b9c79ec854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390371} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe07bb0-ff2d-54fa-ba57-0a37b56d9acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390368}] :question/id #uuid "1a05ecba-dbf9-513d-af2d-03ee8f54c56e" :question/math-academy-id "q-20508" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8326c365-38e8-509f-ba26-6de3d26a5411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390376} {:answer/id #uuid "f0893938-c4dc-5b69-ac7a-20d7546db3b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390377} {:answer/id #uuid "98de7d9c-ac96-50b3-a7cd-2e1f0a084bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390378} {:answer/id #uuid "5d46c30a-315a-5f3c-9e1c-febc548b0a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390379} {:answer/id #uuid "c961a688-8a1a-5a32-8996-3f5dbb760b72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390377} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a2efbab-ca3d-5dfb-bdbf-f29fc5964e47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390375}] :question/id #uuid "4b0ab2ea-5bc8-5361-b6e4-ca31cdf1350a" :question/math-academy-id "q-20539" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 9 & -13 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 9 & -13 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395769 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23b6f110-fbc4-5322-8a05-6366ff4c13c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,4,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395771} {:answer/id #uuid "e6302263-6554-5d2f-bdfe-094ceb26b042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395772} {:answer/id #uuid "337c9891-a990-5356-ae53-39e28e060932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395773} {:answer/id #uuid "12ab6864-c814-589e-8f72-328eeae44af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨13,-4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395774} {:answer/id #uuid "fa67123d-ee59-563d-90e5-5d86c85b1243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-11,4,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395773} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a758e48-dc27-560b-a0af-fd01b7ea572b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395770}] :question/id #uuid "3437106d-95df-5058-942b-4f64c5179bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-20512" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ 2x+3y+4z &=6 \\\\ 3x+3y+4z &=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ y &=4 \\\\ z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=4$ and $z=-4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(4)+2(-4)=1\\,⟹\\,x=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5,y=4$, and $z=-4.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨5,4,-4⟩.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096673 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096460 :question/id #uuid "7760b6ce-91fb-5ba6-beb2-c244d6a73d69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4702" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/cd/cd75b39fc76773c0b3938ab6d60651e2b08dcd9ac325cc05718837934130ea07.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](images/93/933b897b7bc067610c87ea50a6fb871f04c5cc4610bd5bb0c868e6ffbac25e86.svg)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/42/42a1d61517661ccff31d9e603df548e79db7b0674a1f7f34c269a3a19e1c4bd6.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1) &=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38b8de74-9b19-5fcb-86d1-d4eb77627541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339638} {:answer/id #uuid "82fe070f-9ba8-572e-807f-b7e3a637c60e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1$, $y=2$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340305} {:answer/id #uuid "98a029ca-6087-5b72-9ca2-e3147cdb70a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=-5$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340507} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e3c2ea-d16f-581b-9b65-22d05f5e48ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=5$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341062} {:answer/id #uuid "e383876d-902d-5a68-82a6-fe6aedf0fd52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1$, $y=-6$, and $z=-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339638} :answer-field/id #uuid "18caed8a-a8c5-5f22-b7e0-3310a888fea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341425}] :question/id #uuid "cdba1d21-3eaf-575a-9b38-07c8181fcd34" :question/math-academy-id "q-73396" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=8 \\\\ -2x+2y-3z &=-11 \\\\ x+z &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=8 \\\\ y-z &=1 \\\\ z &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5) &=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5) &=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be1e7bb8-9a1e-5458-a964-4b0a507198e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096025} {:answer/id #uuid "f02adf80-ad51-5b77-9de2-17a4ecf16d77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096026} {:answer/id #uuid "055acce7-97cc-5db6-81ee-578ba34b19f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096027} {:answer/id #uuid "27935cd7-d828-53cd-bfc0-5f4b23f2869f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096028} {:answer/id #uuid "719ae79d-13da-5b25-8d45-65e4a648f56b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096029}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e780d91d-a5fd-57ae-9a3e-87dfda8e42d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096024} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "affc0ad4-801a-5399-8a47-b7526facc7d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403628} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb21bbb-79ee-5df3-9904-5df560da18c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403629} {:answer/id #uuid "c5805566-431b-59b1-b5d4-027282fdf8a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403630} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4c1b86-80d7-59f5-af00-319d8bf12b68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403631} {:answer/id #uuid "76bc4cc9-6acc-5be4-bff8-66f385a06fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403631} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15e152b-e602-5625-9a15-cb468ccf6dd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403627}] :question/id #uuid "e85abf79-3b58-57ed-b3d6-9f31cc3b2817" :question/math-academy-id "q-73397" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "543df558-b8a5-545b-b160-2fe37379c9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263727} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb8ac6b-fce4-57dc-8d57-746bdda1d0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263931} {:answer/id #uuid "c42f8e88-729f-5ad1-b070-bff1132c48a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264714} {:answer/id #uuid "c483a5fe-745e-59db-8de7-5c8a3454d240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264721} {:answer/id #uuid "d70a50c5-13c6-5393-8129-945ea4016aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263931} :answer-field/id #uuid "091832d1-1a63-50c1-8342-a7864cc522dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265260}] :question/id #uuid "f61c846d-507f-5371-aeef-030ef902e9e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130928" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{7}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d3cb3a6-9b25-5f14-b7fe-ef0f81082c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=9$, $y=9$, and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339832} {:answer/id #uuid "6637df9f-50f4-58dd-8cf1-2dded102c657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340027} {:answer/id #uuid "82ffd466-0e67-5425-9c00-af468a2c3588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-89$, $y=-47$, and $z=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340306} {:answer/id #uuid "af2f918c-cf0f-5b21-8e87-4c608c0f9852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-33$, $y=-15$, and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340724} {:answer/id #uuid "c76cf58e-617a-5441-8169-40443447226f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=142$, $y=85$, and $z=22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340027} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf34cc2-5873-5eaf-970b-9dc56a73754a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341457}] :question/id #uuid "4fabb78b-3a40-50c6-9149-8d79603a31f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73579" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+6y-3z &=18 \\\\ -4x+8y-3z &=2 \\\\ y-4z &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=-6 \\\\ y-4z &=-3 \\\\ z &=-22,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-22$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4(-22) &=-3\\,⟹\\,y=-91.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-91$ and $z=-22$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2(-91)+(-22) &=-6\\,⟹\\,x=-166.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c85a87-f9d3-5992-bd65-769c46e1d92d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,-8,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339203} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbe2b87-90d4-5154-8a7b-4cbe5d76ee8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339272} {:answer/id #uuid "266e54c3-4543-5283-9017-83d16e10e193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨25,-18,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339463} {:answer/id #uuid "32af4883-fe55-53ee-8722-a0f084a72e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339575} {:answer/id #uuid "79208760-a400-5994-ac65-f0b5469feeb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-17,12,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339272} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0944fb0-08b1-53ae-b7d8-bc6730da208f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341713}] :question/id #uuid "3624bdf6-d1bf-5873-8a2a-1542d72f9250" :question/math-academy-id "q-73584" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z &=3 \\\\ y+5z &=-8 \\\\ z &=4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5(4) &=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-28$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(-28)-2(4) &=3\\,⟹\\,x=39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=39$, $y=-28$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form $⟨39,-28,4⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f84b955-e25e-5955-8a2a-87d8b550463b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨52,21,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339543} {:answer/id #uuid "304cea0c-89a4-55c8-b0d0-dffbc12bb18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339549} {:answer/id #uuid "35874527-0d05-510c-938e-52c64b49f406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339602} {:answer/id #uuid "57014e05-78ee-56aa-a36c-1a4147653d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} {:answer/id #uuid "e70f0c3f-b109-5746-a6d9-5b910dad1d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5f662ab-5ce0-5cde-8194-11854041cc57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341727}] :question/id #uuid "8a6417a9-7e20-54a9-9651-61368745cde5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73588" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z &=-2 \\\\ y+2z &=-1 \\\\ z &=11,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=11$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(11) &=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-23$ and $z=11$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-23)+3(11) &=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-58.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-58$, $y=-23$, and $z=11.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-58,-23,11⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061b84d7-0a88-5827-a09a-0ae94645e28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339179} {:answer/id #uuid "3493c0b1-471a-5165-b338-34b981a66bfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339595} {:answer/id #uuid "3670b23e-82b8-5a09-8d82-457c528c5b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339614} {:answer/id #uuid "b35d9857-7680-5d0d-9437-cc48d8d3277a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340757} {:answer/id #uuid "bd407622-a505-57f5-ad35-f323345504ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339179} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa4b0ec2-bc66-5a30-b57d-09c5803067da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341676}] :question/id #uuid "7ecd0e17-9926-5c80-9527-2ab263ac9de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73592" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-6y+3z &=-6 \\\\ 2x-4y+3z &=-1 \\\\ 2y-4z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9341f62-c8f8-570d-80c8-63278f533fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=4$, and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368711} {:answer/id #uuid "cf00639b-8c94-5353-94da-3f2b856bf365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368712} {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} {:answer/id #uuid "3baa2212-ba77-51f2-be2f-5e043a5564f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=10$, $y=3$, and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368714} {:answer/id #uuid "da3d5251-f525-5757-9a3a-816f522e1513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=16$, $y=5$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8d2c28-de03-52ea-8fb5-2bfbbb958a9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368710}] :question/id #uuid "3f809106-1e50-5a91-813a-0a376c6d5c21" :question/math-academy-id "q-73587" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=1 \\\\ y-z &=-4 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(1) &=-4\\,⟹\\,y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3(-3) &=1\\,⟹\\,x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e0739b-acd3-5213-baab-e978002551c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=6$, and $z=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400515} {:answer/id #uuid "09aec1aa-dcc4-5694-820b-48b65b045141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400516} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea67907-7f4c-52b6-b879-e7a1aaa740f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=-10$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400517} {:answer/id #uuid "06e6ab1e-4b01-5e52-ba1d-2553cc1a9411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-6$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400518} {:answer/id #uuid "fc215d6c-0ef8-5f56-9172-bb0f8dae360e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=18$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400516} :answer-field/id #uuid "924e4677-652c-5aa5-ad82-4e9a728fb938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400514}] :question/id #uuid "8eff9d12-5ab8-5d85-973e-0e821294f176" :question/math-academy-id "q-130927" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=4 \\\\ -3x-6y+4z &=-8 \\\\ 3x+7y-z &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=4 \\\\ y+2z &=-2 \\\\ z &=4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(4) &=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-10$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(-10)-(4) &=4\\,⟹\\,x=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403654 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbb2c9b-2424-5248-830c-2c1f0a65a08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403656} {:answer/id #uuid "090537bb-6f40-5836-9945-a970355e758b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403657} {:answer/id #uuid "fab64420-cace-555b-aa98-7c62e22daa9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403658} {:answer/id #uuid "bb59ea2b-37e2-5ba0-85a8-5281bf3bc593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403659} {:answer/id #uuid "24b18c66-2b96-5dd6-a905-03f61b72ec8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403659} :answer-field/id #uuid "45e63128-e41c-54ad-afda-6808e4f902e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403655}] :question/id #uuid "09ed8746-0452-52a7-a619-929b2d587f13" :question/math-academy-id "q-73580" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1111935c-e645-5bcc-9a24-5310e4abf00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414019} {:answer/id #uuid "48cbaac4-0396-5dd0-87a0-2f04eaf0760f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414022} {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} {:answer/id #uuid "8b765cfb-d1ea-559d-a6ff-8457bb546f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414025} {:answer/id #uuid "979ac4ef-5db7-5cde-816c-7fb542951f8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa000c8-106a-5c36-ab34-ed3791f10731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414030}] :question/id #uuid "db1a0a35-4ef3-5f5a-8985-ee685a957f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73593" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+6y-3z &=-1 \\\\ -2x-12y+8z &=1 \\\\ -x-5y+4z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1048 :topic/title "Solving 3x3 Systems of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}]}
